  nesnd_chen.1.z: "Keep the existing arrangements."
- nesnd_chen.guard_tt: "Pay @money!#v 12,000#!, then @money!#v 500#! per week and #v 40#! [concept_authority] for six months. Death/wounding/escape weights for this plot: #v 15/25/60#!."
- nesnd_chen.residence_tt: "Pay @money!#v 24,000#!, then @money!#v 1,000#! per week and #v 80#! [concept_authority] for six months. Death/wounding/escape weights: #v 10/20/70#!."
- nesnd_chen.intel_tt: "Pay @money!#v 18,000#!. Armed Forces [concept_approval]: #n −2#! for six months. With an active guard and investigation, death/wounding/escape weights are #v 8/22/70#!.\n\nThe investigation lasts at most six months. Withdrawing the guard, Chen's death, or resolution of this plot ends it as well. Guard expiry, departure or the end of the Ming-Wu crisis is cleaned up at the next monthly review or dossier maintenance; the investigation reduces risk only while a guard is active. Renewing the guard does not extend the investigation."
+ nesnd_chen.guard_tt: "Pay @money!#v 12,000#!, then @money!#v 500#! per week and #v 40#! [concept_authority] for six months. Death/wounding/escape chances for this plot: #v 15/25/60#!."
+ nesnd_chen.residence_tt: "Pay @money!#v 24,000#!, then @money!#v 1,000#! per week and #v 80#! [concept_authority] for six months. Death/wounding/escape chances: #v 10/20/70#!."
+ nesnd_chen.intel_tt: "Pay @money!#v 18,000#!. Armed Forces [concept_approval]: #n −2#! for six months. With an active guard and investigation, death/wounding/escape chances are #v 8/22/70#!.\n\nThe investigation lasts at most six months. Withdrawing the guard, Chen's death, or resolution of this plot ends it as well. The investigation’s protection ends when the guard expires, Chen leaves the country or the Ming-Wu crisis ends. Renewing the guard does not extend the investigation."
  nesnd_chen.3.t: "Minister Chen Wounded"
  nesnd_chen.3.d: "Chen Dongyang was attacked aboard the vessel carrying him east to lecture. A shot passed through his shoulder and arm. His attendants took him below and summoned a physician. Only after nightfall did his waiting students hear that he was still alive.\n\nThe veteran of the Western Qin revolution and the southern reforms now lay wounded. His followers published accounts of the attack and demanded an inquiry into the escort. Provincial correspondence questioned the Southern Command’s shipping arrangements, adding the bloodshed to the struggle over reform and political authority."
  nesnd_chen.3.f: "Take the boundless world as the outer wall, and the right path as the inner city.\n— Chen Dongyang, On the Great Nation"
--- base/localization/english/replace/zzzzzz_nesnd_cne_confidence_l_english.yml
+++ candidate/localization/english/replace/zzzzzz_nesnd_cne_confidence_l_english.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+l_english:
+ nesnd_cne_confidence_journal:0 "The Imperial People’s Confidence"
+ nesnd_cne_confidence_journal_reason:0 "The Great Revolution has passed, but its promises still guide clerks, junior officers, soldiers and peasants. They see the land revolution as the continuation of an unfinished cause.\n\nThe Empire is not the republic envisioned by the young scholars and soldiers of 1810. Republican exiles in the south and northwest call Mu Zhongtang a traitor. Yet many still regard him and his companions as heirs of the Enlightenment movement and champions of progress. Their enthusiasm sustains the reform, even as each new demand tests their patience."
+ nesnd_cne_confidence_status:0 "The public still sustains reform, but its patience is finite. At #v 500#! confidence the republicans rise; at zero, the land revolution fails. Declaring bankruptcy costs #n 500#! confidence."
+ NRP:0 "Han Republican Army"
+ NRP_ADJ:0 "Republican"
+ nesnd_cne_republic_restored_name:0 "Han Commonwealth"
+ nesnd_cne_republic_army:0 "Republican Salvation Army"
+ nesnd_republic_commander_first:0 "Chengzhi"
+ nesnd_republic_commander_last:0 "Han"
+ dp_nesnd_cne_republic:0 "Republican Uprising"
+ nesnd_cne_republic_war:0 "War for the Han Commonwealth"
+ nesnd_cne_republic_journal:0 "Rebuild the Han Commonwealth"
+ nesnd_cne_republic_journal_reason:0 "Republican promises once united scholars, soldiers and villagers beneath one banner. The restoration of an imperial throne divided those comrades into rulers, subjects and exiles. Now the republicans have risen again to complete the unfinished revolution.\n\nThis war cannot end in a lasting partition. Unless the republican armies overthrow the imperial government, their provincial coalition will crumble. If they seize most of its provinces, they can inherit the Empire and proclaim the Han Commonwealth."
+ nesnd_cne_republic_status:0 "While at war with the Empire, directly control at least #v 80%#! of its states to annex it and restore the Commonwealth. Both sides demand annexation.\nIf the war ends while the Empire still exists, the republican cause fails and its territory is annexed by the Empire. Victory grants claims on the parts of Hunan, Hubei and Sichuan outside the Commonwealth and its subjects."
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.1.t:0 "The Old Banners"
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.1.d:0 "Republicans in the north have risen. Officers and provincial organisers have proclaimed the Han Republican Army, accusing the court of betraying the Great Revolution. The people who once sustained land reform are dividing against one another."
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.1.a:0 "Gather the armies still loyal to the court."
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.2.t:0 "For the Republic Again"
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.2.d:0 "The provincial coalition has taken up arms. Its government rejects the imperial throne and pledges to rebuild the Han Commonwealth. Some officers remember marching beside Mu Zhongtang; now their banners advance against his Empire."
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.2.a:0 "Let the republican promise endure."
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.3.t:0 "The Han Commonwealth"
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.3.d:0 "The imperial government has fallen. The republicans have taken over its provinces and offices and proclaimed the Han Commonwealth. The assembly renews its claims to the southern territories still beyond its authority."
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.3.a:0 "Rebuild the Commonwealth."
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.4.t:0 "The Republicans Submit"
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.4.d:0 "The republican coalition can no longer sustain its war. Its provinces return to imperial rule. The fighting has ended, though the questions raised by the rebels remain."
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.4.a:0 "Restore the provincial administration."
+ dp_nesnd_cne_republic_desc:0 "The Empire and republicans contest the northern provinces."
+ dp_nesnd_cne_republic_tooltip:0 "Both sides demand annexation of their opponent."
+ nesnd_cne_delta_land:0 "Land commercialisation"
+ nesnd_cne_delta_urban:0 "National urbanisation"
+ nesnd_cne_delta_estates:0 "Provincial military estates"
+ nesnd_cne_delta_consolidation:0 "Stable livelihoods"
+ nesnd_cne_delta_distress:0 "Livelihood crisis"
+ nesnd_cne_delta_admin:0 "Bureaucracy deficit"
+ nesnd_cne_delta_turmoil:0 "National turmoil above 25%"
+ nesnd_cne_delta_war:0 "War"
+ nesnd_cne_delta_bankruptcy:0 "Bankruptcy"
+ nesnd_cne_delta_appeals:0 "Provincial petitions"
+ nesnd_cne_conf_base_desc:0 "Fading revolutionary fervour"
+ nesnd_cne_conf_radicals_desc:0 "Radicals above 15%"
+ nesnd_cne_conf_intelligentsia_desc:0 "Intelligentsia in government"
+ nesnd_cne_conf_petty_bourgeoisie_desc:0 "Petite Bourgeoisie in government"
+ nesnd_cne_conf_trade_unions_desc:0 "Trade Unions in government"
+ nesnd_cne_conf_industrialists_desc:0 "Industrialists in government"
+ nesnd_cne_confidence_bar_desc:0 "Public confidence: #v [JournalEntry.GetCurrentBarValue(ScriptedProgressBar.Self)|0] / 1000#!"
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.5.t:0 "Embers of the Revolution"
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.5.republic:0 "The monarchy has ended, and with it the political settlement behind Emperor Mu’s land revolution. The new government inherits the offices and their records; the future of fields, towns and military estates now rests with a different order."
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.5.war:0 "Revolutionary civil war has broken out. Provincial offices and armies follow rival governments. Military orders have replaced the programme of surveys and resettlement, ending the court’s land revolution."
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.5.coup:0 "A coup has changed the balance of power at court. Reform officials have been recalled and the provinces await new orders. The movement begun in Emperor Mu’s name has lost its political foundation."
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.5.exhausted:0 "The enthusiasm of the Great Revolution has faded. Officials will no longer promise another transformation; soldiers and villagers no longer trust the assurances they once embraced. The court can still issue orders, but the movement has spent its strength."
+ nesnd_cne_confidence.5.a:0 "Withdraw the decree and end the reform."
