+ nesnd_cne_urban_stop_button_desc:0 "Suspend the state-sponsored resettlement and urban expansion programme."
  nesnd_cne_camps_journal:0 "Ending Military Estates"
  nesnd_cne_camps_journal_reason:0 "Since 1444, the Qin military colonies developed into an estate system across the north. Land funded the army, while the army supported taxation and conquest. Bringing these estates into civilian production challenges entrenched military interests. Provinces may proceed separately, or pause when disputes become too severe."
- nesnd_cne_land_status:0 "Agricultural development supports the transfer of land.\n$nesnd_cne_land_requirements$\nFinal consolidation also requires Peasant Proprietorship, Commercialized Agriculture or Collectivized Agriculture. While active: #p +0.25#! monthly reform progress. Lost agricultural prerequisites or a pause end these benefits."
- nesnd_cne_urban_status:0 "Towns require industry and welfare to absorb population.\n$nesnd_cne_urban_requirements$\nWhile active: #p +0.35#! monthly reform progress. Losing industrial or welfare prerequisites pauses the programme.\n#tooltippable #tooltip:[ROOT.GetCountry.GetTooltipTag],nesnd_cne_consolidation_rules Employment, education and welfare consolidation#!#!\nFunding proposals identify the state before payment."
- nesnd_cne_camps_status:0 "Active estate programmes: #v [ROOT.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('nesnd_cne_camps_active').GetValue|0]#!. Each adds #p 0.05#! reform progress monthly and its own military opposition.\nEach state can be started or paused separately. All temporary effects end with the parent reform."
- nesnd_cne_start_requirements:0 "The reform is active; bureaucracy is non-negative, the country is not bankrupt, disorder is below 65, and the state is still owned."
+ nesnd_cne_land_status:0 "$nesnd_cne_land_requirements$\nEstablish peasant proprietorship, commercialised agriculture or collectivised agriculture."
