- nesnd_land_rules_link:0 "Construction and political effects are listed in the three sub-journals.\n#tooltippable #tooltip:[ROOT.GetCountry.GetTooltipTag],nesnd_land_rules Current living conditions#!#!"
- nesnd_land_rules:0 "Unemployed workforce: #v [Country.MakeScope.Var('nesnd_reform_unemployment').GetValue|%1]#!\nFood-insecure workforce: #v [Country.MakeScope.Var('nesnd_reform_starving').GetValue|%1]#!\nWorkforce household living standards: #v [Country.MakeScope.Var('nesnd_reform_sol').GetValue|1]#!\nMarket access: #v [Country.MakeScope.Var('nesnd_reform_access').GetValue|%1]#!\n\nActive programmes add reform progress; pausing preserves progress already earned."
- nesnd_reform_completion_tt:0 "Reach #v 100#! reform progress, sustain the institutional and living-condition requirements for #v 12#! months, keep disorder below #v 50#!, and avoid a successful coup."
- nesnd_reform_failure_tt:0 "A coup succeeds during the reform, or prolonged severe disorder and deprivation cause a crisis."
- ce_cne_land_reform_goal:0 "Pursue the reform programmes, improve institutions and living conditions, and sustain the gains for twelve months."
+ nesnd_land_rules_link:0 "In Emperor Mu’s grand design, the Empire pursues three revolutionary aims: #bold $nesnd_cne_land_journal$#!, #bold $nesnd_cne_urban_journal$#! and #bold $nesnd_cne_camps_journal$#!.\n#tooltippable #tooltip:[ROOT.GetCountry.GetTooltipTag],nesnd_land_rules This month’s livelihoods#!#!"
+ nesnd_land_rules:0 "Unemployed workforce: #v [Country.MakeScope.Var('nesnd_reform_unemployment').GetValue|%1]#!\nFood-insecure workforce: #v [Country.MakeScope.Var('nesnd_reform_starving').GetValue|%1]#!\nWorkforce household living standards: #v [Country.MakeScope.Var('nesnd_reform_sol').GetValue|1]#!\nMarket access: #v [Country.MakeScope.Var('nesnd_reform_access').GetValue|%1]#!"
+ nesnd_reform_completion_tt:0 "Reach #v 100#! reform progress, maintain sound livelihoods and institutions for #v 12#! consecutive months, and keep local disorder below #v 50#!. The monarchy must remain, confidence must endure, and no coup or revolutionary civil war may have occurred."
+ nesnd_reform_failure_tt:0 "The reform fails if confidence runs out, monarchy ends, a native revolution or secession erupts, or a coup succeeds. Extreme crisis also causes failure: at least fifteen monthly samples, twelve consecutive distressed months, disorder of 90, national turmoil above 40%, legitimacy below 25, and war or a bankruptcy penalty."
+ ce_cne_land_reform_goal:0 "Advance land commercialisation, urbanisation and military-estate reform, and consolidate the land revolution."
  nesnd_reform_status_healthy:0 "#p Reform gains are consolidating#!: #v [ROOT.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('nesnd_reform_good_months').GetValue|0]#! consecutive qualifying months.\n$nesnd_land_rules_link$"
- nesnd_cne_consolidation_rules:0 "#bold Consolidation#!\nSchools level #v 2#!, literacy #v 48%#!, unemployment at most #v 6%#!, food insecurity at most #v 8%#!, living standards at least #v 11#! and market access at least #v 85%#!. Social Security level #v 2#! and living standards #v 12#! allow up to #v 12%#! unemployment. Non-negative bureaucracy, peace and no bankruptcy penalty are required.\n\n#bold Local deprivation#!\nStates with at least #v 500,000#! inhabitants interrupt consolidation after six months above #v 20%#! unemployment, #v 25%#! food insecurity or #v 10%#! severe starvation. National and local rates use workforce; subsistence workers are employed.\n\nComplete at #v 100#! progress, #v 12#! consecutive qualifying months and disorder below #v 50#!. The existing rapid-reform reward still requires completion within 48 months, at least 24 consecutive qualifying months and disorder below 30."
+ nesnd_cne_consolidation_rules:0 "#bold Consolidation#!\nSchools level #v 2#!, literacy #v 48%#!, unemployment at most #v 6%#!, food insecurity at most #v 8%#!, living standards at least #v 11#! and market access at least #v 85%#!. Social Security level #v 2#! and living standards #v 12#! allow up to #v 12%#! unemployment. Non-negative bureaucracy, peace and no bankruptcy penalty are required.\n\n#bold Local disorder#!\nStates with at least #v 500,000#! inhabitants interrupt consolidation after six months above #v 20%#! unemployment, #v 25%#! food insecurity or #v 10%#! severe starvation. National and local rates use workforce; subsistence workers are employed.\n\nComplete at #v 100#! progress, #v 12#! consecutive qualifying months and disorder below #v 50#!. The existing rapid-reform reward still requires completion within 48 months, at least 24 consecutive qualifying months and disorder below 30."
--- base/localization/english/replace/zzzzz_nesnd_south_journal_ui_l_english.yml
