@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
  nesnd_south_monarchy_ended_tt:0 "This country has abolished #v monarchy#!."
  nesnd_south_pressure_bar_desc:0 "Succession Pressure: #v [JournalEntry.GetCurrentBarValue(ScriptedProgressBar.Self)|1] / 100#!  #tooltippable #tooltip:[JournalEntry.GetCountry.GetTooltipTag],nesnd_south_pressure_detail_tt Changes#!#!"
  nesnd_south_compact_bar_desc:0 "Federal Compact: #v [JournalEntry.GetCurrentBarValue(ScriptedProgressBar.Self)|0] / 100#!  #tooltippable #tooltip:[JournalEntry.GetCountry.GetTooltipTag],nesnd_south_compact_detail_tt Conditions#!#!"
- nesnd_south_pressure_detail_tt:0 "#bold Succession pressure#!: #v [Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nesnd_south_pressure_value')|1] / 100#!\nCurrent monthly net change: #v [Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nesnd_south_monthly_pressure_value')|1]#!. Base growth is #n +3#!, or #n +2.5#! under the Federal Compact modifier. Valid reconciliation separately subtracts #p 3#!.\n\nThe attempt on Chen can occur from #v July 1837#! above #v 24#! pressure, and is initiated by #v early 1838#! if still unresolved and Chen is present. Death adds #n 25#!, wounding #n 10#!, and escape #n 3#!.\n\nAfter the case, early accession is available at #v 70#! pressure. Automatic accession requires #v 100#! and Zheng Qin’s departure, or the #v early-1839#! crisis deadline. An unresolved crisis reaches #v 100#! at that deadline and proceeds to accession, provincial replies and confrontation. Completed peaceful settlements are preserved."
- nesnd_south_compact_detail_tt:0 "#bold Federal Compact#!: #v [Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nesnd_south_compact_value')|0] / 100#!\nThere is no automatic monthly progress. Each renewal adds #p 20#! progress and reduces succession pressure by #p 8#!, with an #v 18-month#! cooldown.\n\nRenewal requires nonnegative [concept_bureaucracy], at least #v 50#! [concept_legitimacy], and the active Wu–Ming controversy. The Federal Compact modifier lasts #v 10 years#!; while active, pressure rises by #n 0.4#! per month. Reaching #v 100#! compact progress preserves the Zhu dynasty and ends this crisis."
+ nesnd_south_pressure_detail_tt:0 "#bold Succession pressure#!: #v [Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nesnd_south_pressure_value')|1] / 100#!\nCurrent monthly net change: #v [Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nesnd_south_monthly_pressure_value')|1]#!. Base growth is #n +3#!, or #n +2.5#! under the Federal Compact modifier. Valid reconciliation separately subtracts #p 3#!.\n\nThe attempt on Chen can occur from #v July 1837#! above #v 24#! pressure, and is initiated by #v early 1838#! if still unresolved and Chen is present. Death adds #n 25#!, wounding #n 10#!, and escape #n 3#!.\n\nAfter the case, early accession is available at #v 70#! pressure. Automatic accession requires #v 100#! and Zheng Qin’s departure, or the #v early-1839#! crisis deadline. An unresolved crisis reaches #v 100#! at that deadline and proceeds to accession, provincial replies and confrontation. "
+ nesnd_south_compact_detail_tt:0 "#bold Provincial accords#!\nMainland, overseas and Japanese commitments account for #v 50%, 30% and 20%#! respectively. Accords last #v 36 months#! and lapse if a signatory changes allegiance or overlord, goes to war, or withdraws.\n\n#bold Settlement by agreement#!\nThe chosen side needs #v 85#! political support, a lead of #v 20#! and #v 12#! consecutive months of compliance. Ming needs #v 75%#! accord support and at least two mainland core signatories. Wu needs #v 80%#!, consent to provincial incorporation and Japanese territorial changes, and a suitable fleet. A settlement ends the succession dispute."
